# LAB10a2: e1m1's start in the `bands` x-ray, each renderer thread's rows a colour, mixing
# out to the picture. A still camera at 480,-352,110, yaw 90, slop with the status bar and
# the gun, in the x-ray: the renderer's 8 threads' bands of rows, a colour a thread, held
# for shot seconds 0 to 5.6, then mixed out to the picture over 5.6 to 6.4 (file 6.6 to
# 7.4). Brightness 0.8. 6.4 s with a second of handle each end; no sound.
#
# The colours follow the thread scheduler: which thread takes which band is decided as
# each frame is drawn, so the colours reshuffle every frame and come out in another order
# on every run. The pixels under them are the same on any number of threads. `threads 8`
# is the film's: the x-ray shows the threads, so their number is part of the picture.
#
# Under V3-39: "Every core draws its own bands of the frame. One thread or eight, the same
# pixels."

map e1m1

duration 8.4
fps 60
size 1920x1080
threads 8

preset slop
hud on
gun on
cvar gamma 0.8

camera fixed 480,-352,110 0,90

xray bands
mix 0 1
mix 6.6 1
mix 7.4 0

events on
sound off
